# Header rules live here, not in netlify.toml, on purpose.
#
# netlify.toml is resolved relative to the site's base directory, and a base
# directory set in the Netlify UI overrides the file. When the two disagree the
# build still succeeds and the headers are simply dropped — which is how this
# site spent several deploys serving `max-age=0` on fingerprinted assets with no
# security headers, with nothing in the log to say so.
#
# _headers is read from the root of the *published output* instead, so it
# applies however the site happens to be configured. Vite copies everything in
# public/ into dist/, which puts this file exactly there.
#
# Rules are listed general first: a later, more specific path wins.

/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()

# Vite fingerprints these, so they can be cached forever.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The city bundles keep stable names and change when the pipeline is re-run.
/data/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=600, must-revalidate
